  "peek-schlaeuche": {
    "title": "PEEK tubing",
    "excerpt": "PEEK (polyether ether ketone) is a high-performance material characterised by excellent resistance to thermal decomposition at high temperatures. PEEK tubing is used in applications requiring exceptionally high stiffness.",
    "body": "PEEK (polyether ether ketone) is a high-performance material characterised by excellent resistance to thermal decomposition at high temperatures.\n\nPEEK tubing is used in applications requiring exceptionally high stiffness. Due to the excellent biocompatibility of PEEK, it is suitable for long-term implants. PEEK is frequently used in catheters, HPLC, 3D printing as well as aerospace and automotive applications.\n\nPEEK can serve as an alternative to steel, aluminium, glass and other polymers.\n\nLow moisture absorption, high abrasion and chemical resistance, biocompatibility, torsional stability and excellent stability at elevated temperatures make PEEK a suitable material for many applications.\n\nDescription – application:\n\n- PEEK, 1/16″ OD x 0.13 mm ID, red – HPLC\n\n- PEEK, 1/16″ OD x 0.18 mm ID, yellow – HPLC\n\n- PEEK, 1/16″ OD x 0.25 mm ID, blue – HPLC\n\n- PEEK, 1/16″ OD x 0.50 mm ID, orange – HPLC\n\n- PEEK, 1/16″ OD x 0.75 mm ID, green – HPLC\n\n- PEEK, OD 4.95 mm ID 4.25 mm, black – laparoscopy\n\n- PEEK Mono, OD 1.75 mm – 3D printing\n\nOther sizes, colours and applications on request."
  },
  "schlauch-zuschnitte": {
    "title": "Tubing cut to length",
    "excerpt": "In industrial electronics, apparatus engineering and the medical technology sector, finished tubing sections with the smallest tolerances are often required for series production. BIT cuts heat-shrink and insulating tubing made of various plastics to individually required lengths – with the highest precision.",
    "body": "In industrial electronics, apparatus engineering and the medical technology sector, finished tubing sections with the smallest tolerances are often required for series production. BIT cuts heat-shrink and insulating tubing made of various plastics to individually required lengths – with the highest precision.\n\nOur strengths in processing tubing lie in maintaining tight length tolerances, high cutting accuracy and flexible implementation combined with very short delivery times.\n\nYour advantages:\n\n- High stock availability of many insulating and heat-shrink tubes\n\n- Flexible implementation from the smallest quantities to series production\n\n- Documentation including works test certificates possible\n\n- Very short delivery times and precise adherence to delivery dates\n\n- Large choice of materials: e.g. PVC, polyolefin, silicone, PTFE, fiberglass\n\n- Thermal cutting to length of braided sleeving\n\n- Special sizes from 3 mm section length possible\n\nOur customers select the required tubing material, e.g. from the areas of heat-shrink tubing, PTFE tubing, silicone tubing or braided sleeving, and define the desired cutting length.\n\nWe realise the individual cutting of our tubing on six production lines that are regularly maintained and certified. This offers our customers maximum reliability for series production.\n\nAre you interested in a quote? Get in touch!"
  },
  "plakat-kabelbinder-wahlplakat": {
    "title": "Cable ties for fastening election posters",
    "excerpt": "For fastening posters to lamp posts and concrete pillars, we recommend our GT cable ties made of polyamide 6.6.",
    "body": "Cable ties for fastening election posters\n\nFor fastening posters to lamp posts and concrete pillars, we recommend our GT cable ties made of polyamide 6.6.\n\nFor attachment to lamp posts, cable ties with a length of 430 mm are usually sufficient. For thicker posts or concrete pillars we offer cable ties up to 1,000 mm in length.\n\nFor double-sided posters with drilled holes, use our 200 mm long cable ties.\n\nFor mounting the election posters we recommend our cable tie tensioning tools. These tighten the cable ties quickly and easily and cut off the protruding end of the cable tie.\n\nTalk to our sales team – we look forward to your inquiry!"
  },
